From 68cc0feebf352c0ed13e9eca33745313481f4bd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cchaduvu <cchaduvu@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:56:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] visp_video: reduce min_queued_buffers from 5 to 3 for ISP 
 Tuning Tool v2.0

The Versal AI Edge Gen2 ISP Tuning Tool v2.0 allocates only 3 video
buffers when capturing frames via the V4L2 interface. The visp_video
driver's vb2 queue was configured with min_queued_buffers = 5, which
causes vb2_core_reqbufs() to enforce a minimum of 5 buffers. When the
tuning tool requests only 3 buffers via VIDIOC_REQBUFS, the vb2
framework silently adjusts the count upward, leading to a buffer count
mismatch that causes the tuning tool to fail silently during streaming.

Reduce min_queued_buffers to 3 so the vb2 queue accepts the buffer
count requested by the tuning tool, allowing it to operate correctly.

Signed-off-by: cchaduvu <cchaduvu@amd.com>
---
 visp_video/visp_video_register.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/visp_video/visp_video_register.c b/visp_video/visp_video_register.c
index c584d28..b2ce8c7 100644
--- a/visp_video/visp_video_register.c
+++ b/visp_video/visp_video_register.c
@@ -2909,7 +2909,7 @@ static int visp_video_queue_init(struct visp_video_dev *visp_vdev)
 	queue->lock = &visp_vdev->video_lock;
 	queue->dev = visp_vdev->visp_mdev->dev;
 
-	queue->min_queued_buffers = 5;
+	queue->min_queued_buffers = 3;
 
 	ret = vb2_queue_init(queue);
 	if (ret) {
